/-
# Arbitrary finite-root corrected-slab conditional stability

The corrected-slab carrier estimate is not intrinsically restricted to the
two central cube roots.  Its general form accepts any finite list of canonical
roots retained by the slab, together with a literal lower bound on the
connected carrier generated by those roots.  This file carries that general
tail through positive normalization, Boolean complementation, and the exact
physical/support-gas bridges.

The resulting two-sided modulus is

    |roots| * (anchorDecoratedEffectiveRatio ^ floor * 2).

It is uniform in the finite character cutoff.  No assertion that a chosen
root chart has a growing floor is made here; that geometric chart-alignment
fact is deliberately an explicit hypothesis.
-/

